Before we start, a moment of silence for the 14+ cavemen killed getting
to this point. Of the 14 recorded:

1) Boron. Killed by Leocrotta which proved to be faster than I had
anticipated.
Leocrottas are lethal - speed 18!  Beware of these. They seem to be
making a number of kills.
2) Killed by giant ant.  Knocks me down to 6.  No prayer, can't
reliably engrave "E"... use wand of missile
as last resort, die when it bounces back.
3) Thag. Finishes the quest and makes it all the way to the valley of
the dead, seemingly a certain
ascension.  He decides to improve his chances by reading books.  One
paralyzes me, and a cockatrice
walks up.
"You are a statue". DYWYPI?
Lesson learned: Read NO book unless certain it is blessed. As a miracle
worker, uncursed.
4. scroll turns to dust in shop, costing more than I can afford.
5. Thag finishes sokoban, is walking out and falls into a pit with
poison spikes. Not poison resistant. die instantly. I don't think this
was truly avoidable.
6. Bog killed by electrical vortex while not shock resistant. Next time
teleport out.
7. Bag chased down and cornered by black unicorn and mumak.
8. Chased down and killed by killer bee.
9. Thig cornered by Mumak. Dodged wrong way.
10. Thog fell through level teleport, cornered by soldier ants and a
shape-changer.
The reader may ask, "Why didn't you engrave E?"   The reason is that my
character had low dexterity
and could not engrave e. He would always miss a letter or two.
11. Thag trapped on square with "E" engraved by leocrotta and fire
ants.
I attempt to add to engraving using gem. I smudge the original, and die
almost instantly.
12. Thog attempts to uncurse an object in a fountain, and unleashes a
water demon, which promptly
gates in Yeenoghu. DYWYPI?
13. Thag killed by premature trap door to big room, fried by Pyrolisk.
14. Thag ascends.

Original character:
Thag: St: 17 Dx: 14 Co: 20 In : 8 Wi: 9 Ch: 7
Dwarf .

Note reasonably high dexterity (allowing me to reliably engrave E) and
high constitution, which
gave me scads of hit points.  Being a dwarf confers infravision -- very
useful in these dark places! Also means that Gnomish mines are a
relative breeze, since all gnomes and dwarfs are peaceful. Of course,
it took
a long time to get a pick-axe ... but I found ways around that.

Other notes:
1) Mind flayers turn out to be fairly simple as long as you can keep
away from them and shoot them with
arrows. I killed 3 of them and 1 master mind flayer at distance with
skilled bow and arrows and they never
laid a tentacle on me.

An especially neat trick was using the bow and arrows while levitating
-- firing an arrow pushes my character back in the equal and opposite
direction. This allowed me to attack the bad guys and run
away at the same time.

Major mistake that almost got me killed: Engraving "E" with a diamond.
While doing this, a centaur came up
and started hitting me -- 3-4 attacks a turn -- for 8 turns until I
finished engraving.  Fortunately, my AC was -38 and thus he did me no
damage.  But if it had been a cockatrice ... I'd have died for sure.

Another thing ... the Astral level wasn't actually hard this time. I
hate to use the word "routine"
when it comes to the Astral plane, but it wasn't really that
challenging.

